  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an **existing upper-upscale hotel asset in Europe**, the most relevant brands to consider are typically **upper-upscale and luxury soft-brands / collections** with strong European recognition and conversion flexibility, rather than strictly limited-service flags.[1][4][10]\n\nA practical shortlist includes:\n\n- **Radisson Blu** — repeatedly identified as Europe’s largest upper-upscale hotel brand, and Radisson Hotel Group notes it has maintained that position with presence across many European cities.[2][3][4]\n- **Marriott’s Autograph Collection** — listed by STR as an **upper-upscale chain** and commonly used for conversion-friendly, independent-style hotels.[1]\n- **Hilton’s Curio Collection** / **Conrad** / **Waldorf Astoria** — Curio is often used for conversion opportunities, while Conrad and Waldorf Astoria sit at the luxury end for stronger assets or repositionings.[6][7][13]\n- **Hyatt’s Andaz** / **Park Hyatt** / **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt** — good fits where the asset has a distinctive design, heritage, or strong local identity.[6][9][13]\n- **IHG’s Kimpton** / **InterContinental** / **Hotel Indigo** — Hotel Indigo is especially relevant for conversion and local-story positioning; InterContinental is a strong upper-upscale/luxury option in key European cities.[6][10][13]\n- **Accor’s MGallery** / **Sofitel** / **Pullman** — strong Europe-heavy platform, with MGallery and Sofitel often relevant for character-driven or premium urban assets.[6][13]\n- **Marriott’s Tribute Portfolio** and **W Hotels** — more design-led or lifestyle-oriented choices where the asset can support a differentiated positioning.[10][13]\n- **Rocco Forte Hotels**, **Kempinski**, **Rosewood**, **Mandarin Oriental**, **Four Seasons**, **Jumeirah**, **Bulgari**, and **Banyan Tree** — these are more selective luxury options, but can be suitable if the asset is truly top-tier in location, condition, and market demand.[7][12][13]\n\nIf you want the answer framed specifically for **conversion-friendly brands** versus **highest-rate luxury flags**, I can rank the best European options into those two buckets.",
